(David R. Jaracz) writes:

>> What do you think is the best wish for a 1st level wizard (or any
>> other character)

For a starting wizard, I'd *never* wish for gray dragon scale mail.  Look,
the only reason you wanted gray was so you could have magic resistance,
right?  And a starting wizard already has magic resistance!  Best to go
for another dragon intrinsic.  I'd take *black* dragon scale mail.

Yeah, yeah, flame breath, I've heard all the arguments about cloak of
displacement & gray dragon scale mail vs. cloak of magic resistance &
black dragon scale mail, but in my playing experience, I've found:

	1) if you don't cheat or do "abuses", you can't always count on
	   getting everything you need
	2) magic resistance and disintegration resistance are *mandatory*
	   intrinsics, and displacement is not (actually, I'm usually
	   invisible and so heavily protected by the time I hit the
	   castle, I don't even miss displacment if I don't have it).

Covering your mandatory intrinsics first leaves you greater flexibility
later in the game.  I *always* want more things than there are wishes for
in the castle's WoW.

		--Bill


